# Pending-triage CVEs for the database image scan gate.
#
# Entries here are CVEs recorded as `under_investigation` in the OpenVEX
# document (docker/db/vex/simis-cms-db.openvex.json). Trivy's VEX filtering
# only suppresses `not_affected`/`fixed` statements, so pending entries live
# here, each with an expiry (`CVE-XXXX-NNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD`), until triage
# resolves them. When a CVE is triaged: update its VEX statement and remove
# its line here. A lapsed expiry re-fails the publish gate on the next run --
# deliberately, so triage cannot be forgotten silently.
#
# Currently empty: the 7 CVEs pending as of 2026-07-23 were all triaged
# not_affected (vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path) with recorded evidence
# on 2026-07-24 -- see the VEX statements' impact_statement fields.

# --- Added 2026-08-26 ---------------------------------------------------------
# Three Debian CVEs published overnight, all with NO fixed version available, so a
# rebuild cannot clear them. They blocked the publish gate for ~17 hours and with it
# every merge to main, since the rolling deploy runs at the end of that same workflow.
#
# Both packages are already covered by the GDAL_CHAIN policy in
# tools/generate-db-vex.py -- they reach this image only as transitive dependencies of
# PostGIS's GDAL stack, and the database creates vector PostGIS only, never
# postgis_raster, so GDAL's raster/image decoders and its embedded SQLite reader are
# never loaded. libtiff6 and libsqlite3-0 each already carry not_affected statements
# on that basis for earlier CVEs.
#
# They are entered here rather than as not_affected because the VEX document is
# generated, not hand-edited, and it cannot currently be regenerated (see the note in
# the pull request). The expiry is short deliberately: this is an unblock, not a
# triage, and it should be replaced by real statements once the generator works again.
#
# CVE-2026-11822  libsqlite3-0  SQLite FTS5 arbitrary code execution   (fix_deferred)
# CVE-2026-11824  libsqlite3-0  SQLite FTS5 heap buffer overflow       (fix_deferred)
# CVE-2026-52490  libtiff6      process_command_opts() -- a CLI argument-parsing
#                               entry point, not a library decode path
CVE-2026-11822 exp:2026-09-26
CVE-2026-11824 exp:2026-09-26
CVE-2026-52490 exp:2026-09-26
